PATCH 567: the T-80 (type 3) cluster that patch 566 switched on -- 97d5's dispatched sub-methods
997d/986e/987b/98fb, its fire step 99a2, the four weapon spawns 0f69:a4ee/a4a9/a533/a585
(= FUN_1000_9b7e/9b39/9bc3/9c15), and the two remaining host-pointer call sites in 97d5.

Producer/consumer, once more: patch 252's DS-relative table1 meant no T-80 ever ran its per-tick
methods, so all of them stayed in Ghidra's pristine form -- the object near offset dereferenced as a
host pointer, the WORD ammo counters read as 4-byte ints, b1df's returned projectile (`mov si,di ;
pop di`: SI = new object, DI = firer) dropped for `unaff_CS`, the clc/stc contract lost, and 99a2's
far dispatch table `lcall DWORD cs:[0x99f4 + [di+0x91]*2]` read as a near call through a string
literal's address.  With 566 in place the first tick of the first T-80 faulted in 986e (SIGSEGV at
0xc559 = a near offset used as a host pointer).

Every function is the twin of an already-patched type-0 one and takes its conventions from it:

    997d  reload countdown [+0xa8] -> [+0xd7]=3           (7d69 / 276-278 class)
    986e  `testb $8,[+0x16] ; movw $0x190,[+0xad]`        (7cb2, patch 278: timer 0xf there, ammo 400 here)
    987b  rack reload loop: word[+0xb1] <- byte[+0xbb] up to 4, bf3c(0x17) per round, gated on
          word[0x6cde]&0xff0 and the [+0x19]&1 arm bit; DI positional in param_1 (Ghidra: param_2)
    98fb  FUN_1000_9ffc(di) (patch 275, near offset) + the [+0x3d]&0xe0 servo reset
    99a2  fire dispatch: gate [+0x91]==6 || [+0xa8]==0, far table 0x99f4, CF -> bf77 / live target
          -> bf94 / muzzle bf3c(byte[0x9246 + [+0x91]>>1])                        (7e29, patches 428/496)
    9b39 9b7e 9bc3 9c15  the spawns                                                (778a 7745 7814 77cf, 429/495)
          9b39: ammo [+0xaf], a265 aim, b1df(0xc), b77d, [+0xa8]=2, 9b5c, c047(3), [+0x92]=0, [+0x3c]=0x10
          9b7e: ammo [+0xad], a265, b1df(0xd), b793, same tail
          9bc3: ammo [+0xb1], NO aim call, b1df(0xb), b6e3(ax = remaining [+0xb1]), [+0xa8]=2, c047(0x18),
                [+0x92]=0, then bfeb with DI = the TARGET when word[+0x97] is a vehicle (type <= 3);
                a b1df failure lands on the clc exit
          9c15: gated `testw $7,[0x6cde]`, ammo [+0xb3], b1df(7), b6c9, [+0xa8]=0, c047(6); clc on failure
    97d5  `call 0x99a2` and `call 0xa57a` with DI = the near offset (patch 496's fix for the 7e29 site;
          the a57a site is the fifth one, missed by patch 562)

The spawn signatures keep Ghidra's arity as patch 495 did (DI in param_4 for the 5-arg 9b39/9b7e, in
param_3 for the 4-arg 9bc3/9c15), and 99a2 threads it per entry the way 7e29 does.

Measured before this patch (AZER1 self-play with 566 alone): SIGSEGV in 986e on the first T-80 tick.
Measured with 562-565 but without 566/567: the three T-80s inert for 15 minutes.  Original: DEFEAT at
5:49 with 10 enemy ground kills.

